encyclopedia :latch_watch do
  name "Latch Watch"
  summary "A latch watch is a neighbor who sits at a household's door for a damped month of lying-in, deep sickness or first mourning, deciding who and what crosses the threshold while the room behind it stays quiet."
  kind :culture
  subkind :social_order
  status :complete
  topics :household, :"social-structure", :resonance, :subject_common_life
  prevalence :rare
  available_globally
  integration "Streets sit one another's latches in turn; midwives and sickroom trades post the need, and a household repays the month when the watcher's own family needs one, sometimes decades later"
  aesthetic "A stool and lap-board beside the door, the latch cord looped over the watcher's wrist, and a hung felt quiet-cloth muffling the knocker"
  log "2026-09-23 — Rebuilt the entry around the watcher's month on the step, the callers it refuses and the street's arguments about it, keeping every fact of the office."

  descriptive_identity(
    appearance: "A neighbor on a low stool by the door, lap-board across the knees and " \
                "the latch cord looped at the wrist, with felt hung over the knocker " \
                "above and a stack of lidded pots on the step.",
    manner: "The watcher talks to every caller at the stool, lifts the lid on whatever " \
            "they carry, writes the message on the lap-board and names a day when the " \
            "caller may come back. The household head leaves the door to the watcher " \
            "for the whole month.",
    hospitality: "Refused callers sit a while on the step with the watcher, trade news, " \
